<LevelHeader>
  type = Level
  name = The Motherlode
  description = 
  timestamp = 133687433958532641
</LevelHeader>
<Tips>
  You want the Pyromancer to attack someone who's standing next to the mana vein, so he ignites it inadvertantly.
  You could stand there yourself, but you also have a way of making him attack his own team.
  Banks recently gained the ability to teleport anyone to a Death's Door she's placed.
  A good turn 1: place a Death's Door on the mana vein, Rabid Bite the Pyromancer, then Death's Floor the enemy he targets.
  Once the stash drops, you need to trick the Pyromancer into igniting that too. Igniting any square adjacent to it is enough.
  Jen and Dall's bodies are by the lower corner of the stash. Have Banks walk through some dust clouds if she needs mana.
  Once both stashes are alight, you need to hold out a few more turns, teleporting one wizard per turn to the roof.
  Folks you blink out will heal up and restock before arriving at the roof. Let's say they blink to a supply room first?
  Jen's a good choice to go first, if you can spare her. Anyone who's out of ability uses, or on fire, is also good.
  You're not trying to win the fight down here, just survive long enough to get your people to the roof.
  If you're struggling, forget heroics: it's not mission critical to save the militia folks. You can always replay later.
</Tips>

